  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch01-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch01-08--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch01-08--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch01-08: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.05" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.048"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "not-empirically-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "This is a conceptual claim about categories. No dataset of organismal properties can show that a clear vital-versus-physical rule is impossible, because any proposed rule can be rejected as unclear without a measurable consequence that separates the claim from a rival rule." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: The claim asserts that there is no clear rule dividing vital from physical properties. A survey of how biologists classify phenomena would describe usage, not confirm or refute the absence of a rule." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Denying a classification does not specify a distinguishing measurement." .
